From: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0025] sensorhub/ssp: regulator_force_disable for a genuine MCU cold-cycle

The bootloader leaves vdd_mcu_1p8 enabled with num_users == 0, so the existing
regulator_disable() is an unbalanced no-op and the rail never physically falls.
A warm reboot therefore never re-enters the BCM47752 boot-ROM autobaud window
and every firmware download reads 0xFFFF.

Use regulator_force_disable() in set_mcu_power()'s `echo 0` path so the rail
actually drops; regulator_enable() (case 1) restores our reference.  This is
ONLY reachable through an explicit, operator-initiated sysfs write, never an
automatic service loop.  The bring-up recovery path's equivalent change is
owned by 0027 (the downloader), not duplicated here.

AUDIT: vdd_mcu_1p8 may be shared with GNSS; force-disable drops every
consumer's reference.  Do not call from periodic/service paths and always
restore with regulator_enable() as part of the same bounded operation.

Signed-off-by: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
---
diff --git a/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_sysfs.c b/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_sysfs.c
index e9004ed3a003..de4c9fb5b0ac 100644
--- a/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/sensorhub/brcm/ssp_sysfs.c
@@ -565,8 +565,23 @@ static ssize_t set_mcu_power(struct device *dev,
 	if (data->regulator_vdd_mcu_1p8 != NULL) {
 		switch (enable) {
 		case 0:
+			/*
+			 * Nuxel: the bootloader leaves vdd_mcu_1p8 enabled with
+			 * num_users == 0, so a plain regulator_disable() is an
+			 * "unbalanced disable" and the rail never physically drops.
+			 * regulator_force_disable() detaches every reference so the
+			 * rail can actually fall; regulator_enable(case 1) then
+			 * re-attaches our reference.  This is ONLY reachable through
+			 * an explicit `echo 0 > mcu_power` sysfs write (a bounded,
+			 * operator-initiated cold-cycle), never an automatic loop.
+			 *
+			 * AUDIT: this rail may be shared with GNSS.  A force-disable
+			 * drops every consumer's reference count; do not call it from
+			 * any periodic/service path, and always follow with a bounded
+			 * regulator_enable() restore as part of the same operation.
+			 */
 			if (regulator_is_enabled(data->regulator_vdd_mcu_1p8))
-				ret = regulator_disable(data->regulator_vdd_mcu_1p8);
+				ret = regulator_force_disable(data->regulator_vdd_mcu_1p8);
 			break;
 		case 1:
 			/*
